{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e706dc9110370d25","name":"The Order of Shasa","source":{"id":"source:reference-e706dc9110370d25","title":"The Order of Shasa","revision":22376,"timestamp":"2024-09-03T14:36:14Z","sha256":"ca8b7f3e551f16266476c7b09b22eaa9551d7b5ea8f0956e1c13a1ac1d53f6a5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22376","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Order%20of%20Shasa&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e706dc9110370d25","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Order of Shasa is a new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Tradition"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Tradition"},", formed just after the end of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"},". Named for its founder, the Order is exclusive to the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manaan","referenceId":"reference:e148d0a9b917e831"}," and its native Species, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Selkath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Selkath","referenceId":"reference:9d55787cc45c5b69"},". Toward the end of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"}," and a number of other young ",{"tag":"a","children":["Selkath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Selkath","referenceId":"reference:9d55787cc45c5b69"}," are lured to the Sith Embassy, where they receive Sith training. Their training is short-lived. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Revan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Revan","referenceId":"reference:9199cff8278e357a"}," intervenes, proving to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"}," and the others that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," are distorting the truth and setting them up to serve as a puppet government under Sith control.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After the war ends, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"}," realizes that if ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manaan","referenceId":"reference:e148d0a9b917e831"}," is to remain truly neutral in the coming years, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Selkath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Selkath","referenceId":"reference:9d55787cc45c5b69"}," must not rely on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," anymore than they rely on the corrupt Sith. However, Force-sensitive ",{"tag":"a","children":["Selkath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Selkath","referenceId":"reference:9d55787cc45c5b69"}," still need training and guidance to develop their powers and avoid ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"}," and the other Sith-trained ",{"tag":"a","children":["Selkath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Selkath","referenceId":"reference:9d55787cc45c5b69"}," develop a doctrine of peace and defense, creating an organization initially known as The Order of Shasa. With few members formally training in the ways of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", the Order rapidly discovers that Dark Side temptations are a constant threat. Those with Sith training have difficulty disregarding their earlier lessons, especially when they were so powerful, useful, and tempting.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Order of Shasa struggles to resolve the conflict between ideals derived from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Light Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Light_Side"}," and techniques based on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", seeking a path of moderation between the light and dark. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," deception fresh in her mind, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"}," has avoided contacting ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," or any other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Tradition"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Tradition"}," for aid. However, if Dark Side proponents make significant advances or begin to influence new members of the Order, she will not hesitate to seek advice from a Jedi she trusts, or from another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Tradition"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Tradition"}," with a good reputation, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jal Shey"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jal_Shey","referenceId":"reference:f5450be28191b38e"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because the Order is so new, initiates undergo little formal training; those teaching have little more experience than those learning. However, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"}," has instituted one formal initiation requirement- the Rite of Fira. Students deemed ready to become full members of the Order are sent on a special quest that serves as a final test of their abilities, reminding them of the reason the Order was founded and providing them with a weapon for personal defense. The Rite of Fira requires the initiate to swim to the wreck of the kolto harvester destroyed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Revan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Revan","referenceId":"reference:9199cff8278e357a"}," in the Hrakert Rift. After removing a piece of metal from its cortosis-laden hull plating, the initiate must then use the heat from volcanic vents on the ocean floor to craft the cortosis into a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fira"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fira","referenceId":"reference:4ec91cc40800019d"},"- a curved, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"-resistant sword, which members of the Order can use to defend themselves against possible Sith- or even Jedi- threats.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Members of The Order of Shasa can select ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," from the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Order of Shasa Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Order_of_Shasa_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:4bbdc487bfc4bf7e"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Order of Shasa Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Heroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Shasa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shasa","referenceId":"reference:0937033b5742489a"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"br","children":[]},"\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
